Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to return the second element of the split string instead of `parts[0]` to return the first element. This caused:
- `first_word('hello world')` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `first_word('solo')` to crash with an IndexError since there's no second element

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`.
